<h2 data-section-id=3D"wcxajk" data-start=3D"41" data-end=3D"50">GitHub</h2=
>
<p data-start=3D"52" data-end=3D"409">GitHub is a web-based platform for ho=
sting and collaborating on software development projects that use the Git v=
ersion control system. It enables individuals and organizations to manage c=
ode repositories, track issues, and collaborate through version-controlled =
workflows. GitHub has become a central hub for open-source software and ent=
erprise development.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"r4ip8y" data-start=3D"411" data-end=3D"424">Key fact=
s</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"425" data-end=3D"696">
<li data-section-id=3D"m4m1pr" data-start=3D"425" data-end=3D"446">
<p data-start=3D"427" data-end=3D"446"><strong data-start=3D"427" data-end=
=3D"439">Founded:</strong> 2008</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1dx4p39" data-start=3D"447" data-end=3D"524">
<p data-start=3D"449" data-end=3D"524"><strong data-start=3D"449" data-end=
=3D"462">Founders:</strong> Tom Preston-Werner, Chris Wanstrath, PJ Hyett, =
Scott Chacon</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"19slz9y" data-start=3D"525" data-end=3D"587">
<p data-start=3D"527" data-end=3D"587"><strong data-start=3D"527" data-end=
=3D"544">Headquarters:</strong> San Francisco, California, United States</p=
>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"tdod64" data-start=3D"588" data-end=3D"640">
<p data-start=3D"590" data-end=3D"640"><strong data-start=3D"590" data-end=
=3D"609">Parent company:</strong> Microsoft (acquired in 2018)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"s2opso" data-start=3D"641" data-end=3D"696">
<p data-start=3D"643" data-end=3D"696"><strong data-start=3D"643" data-end=
=3D"653">Users:</strong> Over 100 million developers (as of 2024)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"1i1brbp" data-start=3D"698" data-end=3D"723">Platfor=
m and features</h3>
<p data-start=3D"724" data-end=3D"1062">GitHub hosts repositories that use =
Git for version control, supporting collaborative development via branching=
, pull requests, and code reviews. It offers issue tracking, project boards=
, wikis, and continuous integration through GitHub Actions. The service is =
available in both free and paid tiers for individuals, teams, and enterpris=
es.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"1wxs8n" data-start=3D"1064" data-end=3D"1093">Commun=
ity and open source</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1094" data-end=3D"1397">GitHub is the primary home for ope=
n-source projects, including major software such as Linux, TensorFlow, and =
React. Its social coding model=E2=80=94where developers can fork, star, and=
 contribute to repositories=E2=80=94has fostered a global developer communi=
ty and accelerated innovation across programming ecosystems.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"spsyk2" data-start=3D"1399" data-end=3D"1436">Busine=
ss model and enterprise use</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1437" data-end=3D"1767">Beyond public repositories, GitHub=
 provides private hosting and enterprise solutions like GitHub Enterprise C=
loud and Server, which integrate with corporate security and compliance sys=
tems. It generates revenue through subscription plans, enterprise services,=
 and developer tools like GitHub Copilot, an AI-powered code assistant.</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"r4tm9y" data-start=3D"1769" data-end=3D"1798">Influe=
nce and integration</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1799" data-end=3D"2061" data-is-last-node=3D"" data-is-onl=
y-node=3D"">GitHub has deeply influenced modern software practices, popular=
izing collaborative version control and DevOps workflows. Its integration w=
ith Microsoft=E2=80=99s developer ecosystem and cloud platform Azure furthe=
r embeds it in the global software development lifecycle.</p></div></div></=
